  "next": "Seven unique roots remain, with eight final unknown leaves and zero failures in 606 complete single probes. A next bounded pair batch derives 177 new clauses and gives three checked SAT leaf terminals, excluded from measured root coverage. Compare bounded checked clause feedback with a larger one-shot allowance, respecting changed-source indexes, acyclic evidence and full root recomposition. For cost, prioritize validated source/intermediate reuse and repeated terminal checking; discovery and cold replay dominate.",
  "outcome": "Checked paired-assumption consequences raise structural coverage 124/138 to 131/138; width nine remains 124/138. Two exposed unique roots plus a repeat close, new unique coverage 15/24 to 19/24, no baseline losses.",
