  "pattern": "Conflict under a first-assumption unit prefix and a second assumption proves a binary clause. Reuse the exact source prefix state across suffixes; persist checked prefix traces once and retain individual suffixes. Adjoin source-checked clauses, run one depth-zero terminal, and lift through original incoming transport.",
  "recognition": "Frequency-ranked signed pairs; 256 attempts and 32 clauses per unknown depth-zero leaf, with no learned feedback during a pass. Restart/shared certificates identical modulo mode; base/width-nine translate exactly to the parent. Of 846 clauses, 691 use suffix conflicts, 123 contradict prefix consequences and 32 have already-conflicting prefixes.",
  "resources": "At depth two, at most 1024 pair attempts and 128 retained clauses per root; at most four additional depth-zero terminal preparations. Shared state stays on one exact source and suffix copies are charged. Prefix pool compression is local, not broader nonconstant residual sharing. Earlier quotas, source reconstruction, checking, persistence and cold replay all charged.",
